class:: Chua
summary:: Three-state RK4 integration of Chua's circuit
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Flows
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/MackeyGlass

description::

Integrates Leon Chua's canonical dimensionless circuit equations with the piecewise-linear diode curve code::h(x) = m1*x + 0.5*(m0-m1)*(abs(x+1)-abs(x-1))::. Fixed init-rate substeps use RK4 and all three raw states are exposed.

Outputs are unnormalized model coordinates and may become large for unstable parameters. Like link::Classes/Integrator::, Chua accumulates state over time; unlike Integrator, it advances a coupled nonlinear three-equation flow with RK4.

subsection:: State-space view

The orbit is intrinsically three-dimensional. The first figure is an oblique projection of code::(x, y, z)::; the second places the orthogonal code::xy::, code::xz::, and code::yz:: phase planes side by side. Together they prevent an appealing camera angle from hiding structure or falsely implying crossings in the full state space.

All figures use the default coefficients, initial state code::(0.7, 0, 0)::, fixed-step RK4, and a discarded initial transient. Each coordinate is fitted independently to make the orbit fill the available plot area.

image::chua-state-space-3d.png#Figure 1. Oblique state-space projection after normalizing the visible ranges. The red, green, and blue arrows show the positive x, y, and z directions.::

image::chua-state-space-projections.png#Figure 2. Orthogonal phase planes from left to right: x-y, x-z, and y-z. The first named coordinate is horizontal.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: alpha
x-equation scale.
argument:: beta
z-equation scale.
argument:: m0
Inner diode slope.
argument:: m1
Outer diode slope.
argument:: x0
Initial x state.
argument:: y0
Initial y state.
argument:: z0
Initial z state.
argument:: timeScale
Dimensionless model time per audio second.
argument:: substeps
Init-rate RK4 substeps, clipped to 1 through 16.
argument:: reset
Restore initial state on a rising edge.
returns:: Three audio-rate outputs: x, y, z.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with one control duration per outer integration step.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ Chua.ar[0] * 0.05 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{
    var state = Chua.ar(timeScale: 6);
    Pan2.ar(state[0] * 0.04, state[1].tanh)
}.play
)
::

subsection:: Real-time state-space sonification

This view receives 30 state samples per second from the same code::Chua:: instance that controls the sound. The server performs only the flow integration, sonification, and bounded-rate code::SendReply:: messages; trajectory storage and drawing remain in the language process. Close the window or press Cmd-period to release the Synth and OSC responder.

code::
(
s.waitForBoot {
    var window, view, synth, trail, project3D, project2D;
    var drawTrace3D, drawTrace2D, replyPath = '/sd/chuaState';
    var maxPoints = 1200;

    ~sdChuaPhaseWindow.tryPerform(\close);
    trail = RingBuffer(maxPoints + 1);

    // Normalize each model coordinate before applying a fixed oblique projection.
    project3D = { |state, rect|
        var nx, ny, nz, px, py;
        nx = state[0] / 2.4;
        ny = state[1] / 0.45;
        nz = state[2] / 4.0;
        px = (nx * 0.72) - (nz * 0.62);
        py = (nx * 0.24) + (nz * 0.29) - (ny * 0.90);
        Point(
            rect.center.x + (px * rect.width * 0.34),
            rect.center.y + (py * rect.height * 0.36)
        )
    };

    project2D = { |state, rect, first, second, firstRange, secondRange|
        Point(
            rect.center.x + ((state[first] / firstRange) * rect.width * 0.43),
            rect.center.y - ((state[second] / secondRange) * rect.height * 0.40)
        )
    };

    drawTrace3D = { |rect|
        var latest;
        Pen.fillColor = Color(0.035, 0.045, 0.075);
        Pen.fillRect(rect);
        Pen.strokeColor = Color(0.18, 0.28, 0.42, 0.7);
        Pen.width = 1;
        trail.do { |state, index|
            var point = project3D.(state, rect);
            if(index == 0) { Pen.moveTo(point) } { Pen.lineTo(point) };
            latest = point;
        };
        Pen.stroke;

        // Redraw the newest part more brightly so motion remains legible.
        Pen.strokeColor = Color(0.25, 0.92, 0.88, 0.95);
        Pen.width = 1.6;
        trail.do { |state, index|
            var point = project3D.(state, rect);
            if(index == (trail.size - 100).max(0)) { Pen.moveTo(point) };
            if(index > (trail.size - 100).max(0)) { Pen.lineTo(point) };
        };
        Pen.stroke;

        if(latest.notNil) {
            Pen.fillColor = Color(1.0, 0.45, 0.25);
            Pen.fillOval(Rect.aboutPoint(latest, 4, 4));
        };
        Pen.color = Color(0.82, 0.88, 0.96);
        Pen.font = Font.sansSerif(14);
        Pen.stringAtPoint("oblique x-y-z projection", rect.leftTop + (12 @ 10));
    };

    drawTrace2D = { |rect, first, second, firstRange, secondRange, label|
        var latest;
        Pen.fillColor = Color(0.05, 0.06, 0.095);
        Pen.fillRect(rect);
        Pen.strokeColor = Color(0.16, 0.20, 0.30);
        Pen.width = 1;
        Pen.line(Point(rect.left, rect.center.y), Point(rect.right, rect.center.y));
        Pen.line(Point(rect.center.x, rect.top), Point(rect.center.x, rect.bottom));
        Pen.stroke;
        Pen.strokeColor = Color(0.74, 0.36, 0.96, 0.82);
        Pen.width = 1.2;
        trail.do { |state, index|
            var point = project2D.(state, rect, first, second, firstRange, secondRange);
            if(index == 0) { Pen.moveTo(point) } { Pen.lineTo(point) };
            latest = point;
        };
        Pen.stroke;
        if(latest.notNil) {
            Pen.fillColor = Color(1.0, 0.45, 0.25);
            Pen.fillOval(Rect.aboutPoint(latest, 3, 3));
        };
        Pen.color = Color(0.82, 0.88, 0.96);
        Pen.font = Font.sansSerif(12);
        Pen.stringAtPoint(label, rect.leftTop + (8 @ 6));
    };

    window = Window("Chua: live state space", Rect(80, 80, 1040, 680));
    view = UserView(window, window.view.bounds)
        .resize_(5)
        .background_(Color(0.018, 0.022, 0.04))
        .frameRate_(30)
        .animate_(true);
    view.drawFunc = { |canvas|
        var bounds = canvas.bounds;
        var main = Rect(20, 48, bounds.width * 0.64, bounds.height - 68);
        var sideX = main.right + 18;
        var sideW = bounds.width - sideX - 20;
        var sideH = (main.height - 24) / 3;

        Pen.color = Color(0.9, 0.94, 1.0);
        Pen.font = Font.sansSerif(18, true);
        Pen.stringAtPoint("Chua trajectory — sound and image share one state", 20 @ 14);
        drawTrace3D.(main);
        drawTrace2D.(Rect(sideX, 48, sideW, sideH), 0, 1, 2.4, 0.45, "x-y phase plane");
        drawTrace2D.(Rect(sideX, 60 + sideH, sideW, sideH), 0, 2, 2.4, 4.0, "x-z phase plane");
        drawTrace2D.(Rect(sideX, 72 + (sideH * 2), sideW, sideH), 1, 2, 0.45, 4.0, "y-z phase plane");
    };

    OSCdef(\sdChuaPhaseView, { |message|
        var sample = message[3..5];
        {
            trail.overwrite(sample);
        }.defer;
    }, replyPath, s.addr);

    synth = {
        var state = Chua.ar(timeScale: 6);
        var frequency = state[0].clip(-2.4, 2.4).linexp(-2.4, 2.4, 90, 1800);
        SendReply.ar(Impulse.ar(30), replyPath, state);
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(frequency, 0, 0.07),
            state[1].clip(-0.4, 0.4) * 2.5
        )
    }.play;

    window.onClose = {
        view.animate = false;
        OSCdef(\sdChuaPhaseView).tryPerform(\free);
        synth.tryPerform(\free);
        ~sdChuaPhaseWindow = nil;
    };
    ~sdChuaPhaseWindow = window.front;
    CmdPeriod.doOnce({ { ~sdChuaPhaseWindow.tryPerform(\close) }.defer });
};
)
::

